{
  "id": "dsmc",
  "title": {
    "ja": "等質DSMC衝突成分の保存則・Maxwell分布",
    "en": "Conservation and Maxwell relaxation in a homogeneous DSMC collision component"
  },
  "method_ids": [
    "dsmc"
  ],
  "summary": {
    "ja": "等質なMaxwell分子のランダム二体衝突で、保存則と平衡分布への緩和を検証します。",
    "en": "Test conservation and relaxation toward equilibrium through randomized pair collisions of homogeneous Maxwell molecules."
  },
  "assumptions": {
    "ja": "等質・等質量・等方散乱・一定衝突率。各roundで全粒子を一度ずつランダムに組み合わせます。初期は±sqrt(3)の二つのビームで、温度の目標は1です。 各seedは総運動量0・総エネルギー固定のmicrocanonical系で、Maxwell/Gammaは大粒子数極限の参照です。",
    "en": "Homogeneous, equal masses, isotropic scattering and constant collision rate. Each round randomly matches every particle once. Two initial beams at ±sqrt(3) give target temperature one. Each seed has zero total momentum and fixed total energy: its finite-N equilibrium is microcanonical, while Maxwell/Gamma are large-N references."
  },
  "algorithm": {
    "ja": "対の重心速度と相対速度の大きさを保持し、相対速度の方向を球面上で一様に選びます。roundは物理時刻ではなく衝突演算の回数です。 D=<vx²−(vy²+vz²)/2>と置くと、ランダムな相方の平均で重心の異方性が(N−2)/(2(N−1))倍になり、散乱後の相対方向の異方性期待値はゼロになるため、保存した期待減衰率が得られます。",
    "en": "Preserve pair center-of-mass velocity and relative speed, then choose the new relative direction uniformly on the sphere. Rounds count collision operations and are not calibrated physical time. For D=<vx²−(vy²+vz²)/2>, averaging a random partner multiplies the center-of-mass anisotropy by (N−2)/(2(N−1)); isotropic postcollision relative directions contribute zero expected anisotropy."
  },
  "validation": {
    "ja": "粒子512・2048・8192、16 seedで、運動量・運動エネルギー、Maxwellの2次/4次モーメント、Gamma(3/2,1)のエネルギーCDFを比較。異方性の期待減衰率(N−2)/(2(N−1))も独立に照合します。 有限Nの成分4次モーメントは3−6/(3N−1)であり、Maxwell値3との有限N偏りとseed間の標本誤差を区別します。",
    "en": "Use 512/2048/8192 particles and sixteen seeds to check momentum/energy, Maxwell second/fourth moments and the Gamma(3/2,1) energy CDF. Independently check the expected per-round anisotropy factor (N−2)/(2(N−1)). The finite-N component fourth moment is 3−6/(3N−1); distinguish that finite-particle offset from the across-seed sampling uncertainty."
  },
  "limits": {
    "ja": "DSMCの衝突部分の教育例です。空間輸送、衝突セル、剛体球の速度依存の衝突選択、実際の輸送係数・流れ場・全seedでの保証は含みません。Bird原著の剛体球条件を再現したとは主張しません。",
    "en": "This is an educational DSMC collision component. No spatial streaming, collision cells, speed-dependent hard-sphere selection, measured transport coefficients/flow fields or every-seed guarantee. Bird’s original hard-sphere conditions are not reproduced."
  },
  "equations": [
    "\\mathbf v_{1,2}^{\\prime}=\\mathbf V\\pm\\frac{|\\mathbf g|}{2}\\mathbf n,\\qquad|\\mathbf n|=1",
    "\\mathbb E[D_{r+1}]=\\frac{N-2}{2(N-1)}\\mathbb E[D_r]"
  ],
  "references": [
    {
      "id": "bird1963",
      "author": "G. A. Bird",
      "year": 1963,
      "title": "Approach to Translational Equilibrium in a Rigid Sphere Gas",
      "doi": "10.1063/1.1710976",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1710976",
      "review_level": "metadata-only",
      "review_note": {
        "ja": "Sandiaの公式DSMC記念文書とDOI書誌を確認。出版社本文は取得できず、原著の剛体球モデルを再現したとは主張しません。",
        "en": "Official Sandia DSMC commemorative document and DOI metadata checked; publisher text unavailable and the original hard-sphere model is not claimed as reproduced."
      }
    }
  ],
